
<% content_for :title, "Third DUI | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="dui-story-page third-dui-page"
      style="--dui-desktop: url('<%= asset_path('addiction_third_dui_desktop.png') %>'); --dui-mobile: url('<%= asset_path('addiction_third_dui_mobile.png') %>');">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="ds-hero">
    <div class="ds-hero-inner">

      <p class="ds-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / ADDICTION / PERSPECTIVES / THIRD DUI
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>THIRD</span>
        <span>DUI.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="ds-intro">
        MANIA.<br>
        IMPULSIVITY.<br>
        THE CONSEQUENCES.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- CONTEXT -->
  <section class="ds-context">
    <p>
      Mania, impulsivity, alcohol, and a malfunctioning interlock.
      This is my account of my third DUI: what I remember,
      what I learned afterward, and what happened next.
    </p>
  </section>


  <!-- STORY -->
  <section class="ds-body">
    <div class="ds-layout">

      <aside class="ds-sidebar">

        <p class="ds-label">02 / MY ACCOUNT</p>

        <h2>
          THE<br>
          MANIC<br>
          EPISODE.
        </h2>

        <div class="ds-note">
          MANIA / IMPULSIVITY / ALCOHOL / BLACKOUT
        </div>

      </aside>


      <article class="ds-copy" aria-label="My third DUI story">

        <!-- THE COFFEE SHOP -->
        <h2>THE COFFEESHOP.</h2>

        <p>
          I could barely sit still at the coffeeshop.
          I had barely slept the night before, thoughts
          racing. I had been daydreaming about all of
          the grandiose ideas and big projects I wanted
          to start and spend a fortune on instead of
          focusing on class. Literally anything to get
          me out of there. I wanted my car back so I
          could drive around for hours, one of the only
          things that calmed me down.
        </p>

        <div class="ds-mania-callout">
          <p>MANIA.</p>
          <span>IT WAS UNMISTAKABLE.</span>
        </div>

        <p>
          <em>Mania</em>
        </p>

        <p>
          It was unmistakable.
        </p>


        <!-- MANIALITE -->
        <h2>MANIALITE™.</h2>

        <p>
          I was upset that my medication wasn't working,
          but it was <em>ManiaLite™</em>. I was still drinking
          on the sly occasionally—or so I thought—at home,
          and the interlock was keeping me sober on the road.
          My consumption had been up more than usual lately
          because of this recent episode, and I was very
          impulsive when it came to drinking.
        </p>

        <p>
          When grocery shopping, I would turn the cart
          on a dime down the beer aisle and just buy
          the booze, not considering any consequences
          at all. It wasn't reflexive—it was something
          I did on a complete whim as if I needed to
          do it or else. I feared it when sober, and
          I had the "fuck its" frequently.
        </p>


        <!-- THE CALL -->
        <h2>THE PHONE CALL.</h2>

        <p>
          Class was going, and I received a call.
          It was the mechanic.
        </p>

        <div class="ds-phone-call">
          <p class="ds-phone-label">THE RECEPTIONIST</p>
          <p>"YOUR CAR IS READY."</p>
        </div>

        <p>
          "Your car is ready," the receptionist said.
          <em>Fucking finally</em>. I logged off,
          gathered my things, and walked over to
          get my car.
        </p>


        <!-- THE INTERLOCK -->
        <h2>THE INTERLOCK.</h2>

        <p>
          I got back into my car, ready to drive away,
          and blew into my interlock as I normally did.
          One blow to start the car, and I expected
          one five minutes in, then one after fifteen.
          Except one didn't come after five minutes.
          Or fifteen.
        </p>

        <p>
          I figured out that the mechanic didn't set
          the interlock back up properly. My vision
          almost went blurry with this revelation,
          as if someone attached jumper cables to
          my already excitable brain that was flopping
          round with activity and thoughts going
          100 mph.
        </p>

        <div class="ds-jackpot">
          <p class="ds-jackpot-main">
            JACKPOT.
          </p>

          <p class="ds-jackpot-sub">
            MY BIPOLAR BRAIN SAID TO ME.
          </p>

          <p class="ds-jackpot-no">
            NO.
          </p>

          <p class="ds-jackpot-sub">
            SAID THE SENSIBLE SIDE OF ME.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          <em>Jackpot</em>, my bipolar brain said to me.
          <em>No</em>, said the sensible side of me.
        </p>

        <p class="ds-guess-who">
          GUESS WHO WON?
        </p>


        <!-- THE DECISION -->
        <h2>THE IMPULSE.</h2>

        <p>
          My mind was spinning like a top, utterly
          focused on alcohol. Nothing else was on
          my brain other than driving the car to
          get somewhere that sold booze and drinking
          that booze. My normal self was screaming
          to stop, but mania had taken over my body.
          I wasn't acting right. I wasn't me.
          It was me, but it wasn't me.
        </p>

        <p class="ds-impact">
          I pulled in to the nearest gas station
          and bought a pack of White Claws,
          and I began to chug.
        </p>


        <!-- BLACKOUT -->
        <div class="ds-blackout">
          <span class="ds-blackout-label">
            THE LAST THING I REMEMBER
          </span>

          <p>
            AND MY MEMORY<br>
            ENDS THERE.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          And my memory ends there.
          I woke up in detox the next day.
        </p>


        <!-- WHAT I LEARNED -->
        <h2>WHAT I WAS TOLD.</h2>

        <p>
          I was told by my lawyer and the police
          report says I hit another car at a
          low speed. No injuries. I was trying
          to commit suicide. My BAC was .28.
          I went to jail for five months,
          and I am still on probation for
          another two and a half years
          out of four for this DUI.
          I did it, and I must pay my
          debt to society.
        </p>

        <div class="ds-consequences">
          <span>BAC: .28</span>
          <span>FIVE MONTHS IN JAIL.</span>
          <span>FOUR YEARS OF PROBATION.</span>
        </div>

        <p class="ds-accountability">
          I DID IT.<br>
          I MUST PAY MY<br>
          DEBT TO SOCIETY.
        </p>


        <!-- FINAL CONSEQUENCE -->
        <h2>THE REALITY.</h2>

        <div class="ds-prison-warning">
          <p class="ds-prison-label">
            THE CONSEQUENCE OF ANOTHER DUI
          </p>

          <p>
            IF I GET<br>
            ANOTHER DUI,<br>
            I GO TO PRISON.
          </p>
        </div>

      </article>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="ds-ending">
    <div class="ds-ending-inner">

      <p class="ds-ending-eyebrow">
        THIRD DUI / THE STORY
      </p>

      <h2>
        THE STORY.<br>
        THEN THE LENSES.
      </h2>

      <p class="ds-ending-copy">
        This experience involved mania, impaired judgment,
        impulsivity, alcohol, and consequences that continued
        long after the blackout. The different perspectives
        examine the circumstances, the decisions, and the
        responsibility that follows.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO ADDICTION PERSPECTIVES",
          addiction_perspectives_path,
          class: "ds-back" %>

    </div>
  </section>

</main>
